/-!
# `Ct`: constant-time proofs for the six-set crate built with `hw-sha2`

The same library as `../lean/Ct` (portable build), over the `hw-sha2` translation. Every file
is a symbolic link to `../lean/Ct`'s file of the same name (and so, where that is a link, to the
main tree's) except the generated `Ct/Funs.lean`, this root, and the build-specific files:

* `Ct/Funs.lean`     GENERATED by `multi/scripts/ct-gen.sh hw` from `Slhdsa/Funs.lean` (header only).
* `Ct/ModelBuild.lean` the build's part of the leakage model (TRUSTED): the main tree's wrapper
                     entries (`../../lean-hw/Ct/ModelBuild.lean`, copied) and this tree's
                     `Slice.index_mut` (`../lean/Ct/ModelBuild.lean`, copied).
* `Ct/CheckTestBuild.lean` name resolution and positive controls for both.
* `Ct/CompressTop.lean` `sha256::compress` and the kernel `compress_block`: a link to the main
                     tree's `../../lean-hw/Ct/CompressTop.lean` (the same functions).
* `Ct/Hw/Lanes.lean` the kernel's rounds: `lane_step`, `lane_tick`, `tick`, `period`, `run`,
                     generic in `N` (adapted from the main tree's).
* `Ct/Hw/Chain.lean` `leave`, `enter`, `chain_all` and its loops, `sha256::hw::chain_blocks`,
                     generic in `N` (adapted from the main tree's).
* `Ct/ChainTop.lean` `hash::chain_blocks`: the portable build's statement, through the kernel.

The headline statements are those of `../lean/Ct/Theorems.lean` and `../lean/Ct/Sets/*.lean`
(links), word for word.
-/
